## Commits
### 843329f
breaking(api): rename onSettled to onIdle

Reserve "settled" for a computation's outcome and name the graph
notification after what it observes: the graph is idle when no effect
is queued and no microtask flush is armed, which can be true while an
async derived value is still pending. The callback type becomes
IdleCallback, graph-side internals say idle (idleCallbacks,
notifyIfIdle, notifyIdleOutsideFlush, MAX_IDLE_CYCLES) and the runaway
error names onIdle. settleProcessed keeps its name because it records
a computation's settlement. Timing is unchanged; a new test pins the
notification that fires while a derived value is pending and again
once it settles.

BREAKING CHANGE: onSettled is now onIdle and SettledCallback is now
IdleCallback. No behavior change.


